## Why This Is Asked

Tests real-world ability to build autonomous, tool-using planning with LangChain, handling failures and idempotence under latency.

## Key Concepts

- LangChain Tools orchestration
- Planning/Autogen style decomposition
- Idempotence and retry semantics
- Observability and testing strategy

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal pseudoplanner
async function planIncident(incident, tools){
  const steps = [];
  if (incident.severity>3) steps.push({name:'fetchMetrics', tool:'metrics_api'});
  steps.push({name:'lookupRunbook', tool:'runbooks_db'});
  steps.push({name:'ensureTicket', tool:'ticket_api'});
  return steps;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test decision paths across edge cases?
- How would you extend to parallel tool execution when safe?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical skills designing a rigorous evaluation framework for a multilingual policy assistant that must ensure every factual claim maps to a live source while detecting cross-source conflicts and tracking policy drift over time.

## Key Concepts

- Multilingual policy alignment and factual consistency
- Versioned source management and drift detection
- Cross-source hallucination detection for conflicting information
- Automated evaluation with comprehensive metrics and tooling

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal verification framework: map claims to source citations
function verifyClaim(claim, sources) {
  const citation = findSourceCitation(claim, sources);
  return {
    claim,
    source: citation.url,
    timestamp: citation.version,
    isValid: validateClaim(claim, citation)
  };
}
```
